        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "1l4fcxuuc5694o2",
                "text": "Review of Electron Configurations and Valence Electrons"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4249638695",
            "type": "h2"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The arrangement of the periodic table is based on the electron configurations. The filling order begins at hydrogen and includes each subshell as you proceed in increasing atomic number (Z) order, as shown in the periodic table below."
              }
            ],
            "id": "385299243",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Periodic table showing orbital subshells for the ground state electron configurations of each element."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1320001349",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "r1c6zmj8h6xdfyv",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "display": "block",
            "id": "2862449623",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/40/406B889BE13A5FC72B4495B7D28E46AD/Electron Configuration Table.jpeg",
            "type": "img",
            "width": 700
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The subshell energy ordering is:"
              }
            ],
            "height": 412.2400817871094,
            "id": "2379493111",
            "type": "p",
            "width": 633.0309847366718
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "1"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 2"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 2"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "p"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 3"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 3"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "p"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 4"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 3"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 4"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "p"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 5"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 4"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 5"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "p"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 6"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 4"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 5"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 6"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "p"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 7"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 5"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 6"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": " < 7"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "2254193109",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Recall that since electron configurations can be long and repetitive and the chemistry is almost entirely due to the outer electrons, it is generally more convenient to write condensed electron configurations. Recall also that metals typically lose electrons and form positive ions, and that electrons are removed from the outer (valence) shell first (not in the reverse filling order). For example, "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "first transition series"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Transition elements in the fourth period of the periodic table (first row of the "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "d"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "-block), atomic numbers 21–30."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2690629632",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4157821812",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " elements (Sc to Zn) typically first lose 4"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "s"
              },
              {
                "text": " electrons to form positive ions before losing 3"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": " electrons, and later "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": "­-block series elements and the "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "f"
              },
              {
                "text": "-block series elements exhibit similar behavior (lose outermost shell electrons first when forming cations)."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3284549299",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "editor": "slate",
        "id": "2701366285",
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "State the condensed electron configuration for (i) a cobalt atom and (ii) a cobalt(II) ion."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1485005875",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Determine the series to which cobalt belongs."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2245165563",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "- - - - -"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1464750224",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cobalt (Co) is element 27 in the periodic table. The electron configuration for Co is: 1"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "6"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "6"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "d"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "6"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and the condensed electron configuration for Co is: [Ar]4"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "d"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "6"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1358882745",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cobalt(II) is a cobalt ion with a +2 charge, Co"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", so it is a Co atom that has lost 2 electrons. The electrons are lost from the outer shell (4"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") rather than the last filled subshell (3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "d"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), so the condensed electron configuration for Co"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is: [Ar]3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "d"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "6"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4129287050",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cobalt is a first transition series element."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3360268126",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "editor": "slate",
