                  }
                ],
                "id": "761880673",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Tungsten(IV) is a tungsten ion with a +4 charge, W"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "4+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", so it is a W atom that has lost 4 electrons. The first two electrons are lost from the highest energy outer shell (6"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") and the next two electrons are lost from the next highest energy subshell (5"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "d"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").  The condensed electron configuration for W"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
